# Emails transactionnels — Resend

> Resend est le service email standard Karibloom. Pour les emails longs (reçus PDF, newsletters) préférer n8n qui a plus de souplesse. Resend = emails courts déclenchés depuis Next.js directement.

---

## 1. Setup

```bash
npm install resend
```

```bash
# .env.local
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...           # server-only, JAMAIS NEXT_PUBLIC_
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@[domaine-client].fr
RESEND_FROM_NAME=[Nom Client]
```

**`lib/resend.ts` — singleton serveur-only :**

```ts
// lib/resend.ts
import { Resend } from "resend";

if (!process.env.RESEND_API_KEY) {
  console.warn("[resend] RESEND_API_KEY manquante — emails désactivés");
}

export const resend = process.env.RESEND_API_KEY
  ? new Resend(process.env.RESEND_API_KEY)
  : null;

export const FROM = `${process.env.RESEND_FROM_NAME ?? "Karibloom"} <${process.env.RESEND_FROM_EMAIL ?? "noreply@karibloom.fr"}>`;
```

Ne jamais importer `resend` dans un fichier `"use client"`. Uniquement dans Route Handlers et Server Actions.

---

## 2. Pattern standard d'envoi

```ts
import { resend, FROM } from "@/lib/resend";

async function sendEmail(to: string, subject: string, html: string) {
  if (!resend) {
    console.warn("[resend] Email non envoyé (API key manquante):", subject);
    return { ok: false };
  }

  const { error } = await resend.emails.send({ from: FROM, to: [to], subject, html });

  if (error) {
    console.error("[resend] Échec envoi:", error.message);
    return { ok: false, error: error.message };
  }

  return { ok: true };
}
```

